35,2,1,talk,Asuka,,Eleven mid-year joiners required hand-worked calculations. Nine taster attendees refused a whole-year commitment. The current structure is administratively heavy and psychologically off-putting.,"{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
36,2,1,talk,Benjamin,,Six hours a month chasing individual payments versus one for a yearly collection. That is not a job; it is a punishment. We cannot expect anyone to volunteer for that.,"{""words"":30,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
37,2,1,talk,Jonathan,,"Eighteen names on no sheet, yet the same nine do all the work. The imbalance is stark. We must address this before setting fees.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
38,2,1,talk,Shunichi,,A third of weekday turnout vanished after a door charge. The quiet ones feel uneasy about per-event costs. We must avoid making attendance feel like a transaction.,"{""words"":27,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
39,2,1,talk,Takumi,,"A third of renewals needed chasing, and seventy percent of costs are fixed. We can’t predict income by guessing. We need a structure that actually collects reliably.","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
40,2,2,talk,Asuka,,"@Benjamin, your hours confirm the administrative burden. @Shunichi, the hesitation is real. We need a structure that is simple to join and easy to collect, without punishing those who attend less.","{""words"":31,""mentions"":[""Benjamin"",""Shunichi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,2,2,talk,Benjamin,,"@Asuka, precisely. The data confirms my fear: per-event collection is unsustainable. We need a method that minimizes the chasing, or we lose the treasurer entirely.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[""Asuka""],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,2,2,talk,Jonathan,,"@Benjamin, the chasing is a symptom. The real issue is that the same nine people carry the entire club. We need to address that imbalance before discussing collection methods.","{""words"":29,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
43,2,2,talk,Shunichi,,"@Jonathan, the imbalance is real, but the hesitation is the immediate threat. If we make attendance feel like a transaction, we lose the people who are already wavering.","{""words"":28,""mentions"":[""Jonathan""],""raw_differs"":false}"
44,2,2,talk,Takumi,,"@Benjamin, you’re right. Chasing money is a nightmare. But @Jonathan, fixing the workload won’t stop the cash flow problems. We need a fee that people actually pay on time.","{""words"":29,""mentions"":[""Benjamin"",""Jonathan""],""raw_differs"":false}"
45,2,3,talk,Asuka,,"@Jonathan, the imbalance is real, but the fee structure must be simple. If joining is too complex, we lose people before they start.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[""Jonathan""],""raw_differs"":false}"
46,2,3,talk,Benjamin,,"@Takumi, the bank data is damning. A third of renewals needed chasing. We need a collection method that doesn’t require a full-time debt collector.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[""Takumi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
47,2,3,talk,Jonathan,,"@Benjamin, the chasing is a symptom of the structure, not the cause. If the fee is fair, the chasing stops. I need to know who is actually here.","{""words"":28,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
48,2,3,talk,Shunichi,,"@Jonathan, the imbalance is real, but the hesitation is the immediate threat. If we make attendance feel like a transaction, we lose the people who are already wavering.","{""words"":28,""mentions"":[""Jonathan""],""raw_differs"":false}"
49,2,3,talk,Takumi,,"@Benjamin, chasing is a symptom of bad design. If we pick a method that collects reliably, the chasing stops. I refuse to guess again.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
50,2,4,talk,Asuka,,"@Shunichi, the taster forms prove people fear the commitment. @Benjamin, the hours prove the work is too heavy. We need a structure that is simple to join and easy to collect.","{""words"":31,""mentions"":[""Shunichi"",""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
51,2,4,talk,Benjamin,,"@Asuka, agreed. Simplicity is the only way to save the treasurer. @Takumi, reliable collection is non-negotiable. We need a method that works for both.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[""Asuka"",""Takumi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
52,2,4,talk,Jonathan,,"@Shunichi, the hesitation is real, but the data shows the core is stable. We need a structure that rewards that consistency without alienating the quiet ones.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[""Shunichi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
53,2,4,talk,Shunichi,,"@Jonathan, the core is stable, but the door is closing. If we make showing up feel like a purchase, we lose the people who are already hesitating.","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[""Jonathan""],""raw_differs"":false}"
54,2,4,talk,Takumi,,"@Benjamin, you’re right. Simplicity saves the treasurer. @Shunichi, I hear you, but we can’t afford to lose the cash flow. We need a balance.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[""Benjamin"",""Shunichi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
